{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כצאת", :translit "k'tzat", :gloss "as the going forth"} {:he "כצאת משה אל האהל", :translit "k'tzat moshe el ha'ohel", :gloss "as the going forth of Moses to the tent"} {:he "כצאת השמש בגבורתו", :translit "k'tzat ha-shemesh bi'gvurato", :gloss "as the going forth of the sun in its might"} {:he "פני משה כפני חמה", :translit "pnei moshe k'pnei chamah", :gloss "the face of Moses is like the face of the sun"} {:he "פועל ביציאתו", :translit "po'el bi'ytzi'ato", :gloss "one who works upon his going forth"} {:he "משל בעה\"ב", :translit "m'shél ba'al ha-bayit", :gloss "of the householder"} {:he "כצאת העבדים", :translit "k'tzat ha'avadim", :gloss "as the going forth of slaves"} {:he "כצאת השמש", :translit "k'tzat ha-shemesh", :gloss "as the sun goes forth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["כצאת" "כצאת משה אל האהל" "כצאת השמש בגבורתו"]} {:kind :other, :note "Phrase-linkage: three verses share identical opening כצאת, read as typologically connected: Moses at tent (Num. 12:8), sun in might (Judg. 5:31), and slave-girl's departure here."}], :frame {:text "The phrase כצאת משה אל האהל appears at Numbers 12:8. The phrase כצאת השמש בגבורתו appears at Judges 5:31, which likens those who love God to the rising sun. Deuteronomy 34:10 records that no prophet arose like Moses. The aphorism פני משה כפני חמה appears as an expansion of the concept that Moses' countenance was solar in radiance, connected to Exodus 34:29–30 where Moses' face shines. The aphorism פועל ביציאתו refers to a laborer's obligation regarding departure times for work, discussed at Bava Metzia 83a where a worker may rise early to walk to distant employment, but his working hours begin only from when the workday starts; Rashi ad loc. invokes the model of free householders who begin labor at sunrise. Ba'al HaTurim applies this labor law to the slave (Exodus 21:7), arguing the Hebrew servant's daily departure is calibrated to sunrise, not before.", :sources ["Numbers 12:8" "Judges 5:31" "Deuteronomy 34:10" "Exodus 34:29-30" "Bava Metzia 83a" "Rashi on Bava Metzia 83a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["כצאת" "כצאת משה אל האהל" "כצאת השמש בגבורתו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "כצאת", :refs ["Exodus 21:7" "Exodus 33:8" "Judges 5:31"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כצאת משה אל האהל", :refs ["Exodus 33:8"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כצאת השמש בגבורתו", :refs ["Judges 5:31"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Phrase-linkage: three verses share identical opening כצאת, read as typologically connected: Moses at tent (Num. 12:8), sun in might (Judg. 5:31), and slave-girl's departure here.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:00.479118028Z", :model "glm-5.2"}